<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 9 July, from 455 to 2011.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">455 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,571 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Avitus is acclaimed Western Roman Emperor near Arles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> and the Gallo-Roman nobility, the senator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avitus">Avitus</a> was acclaimed emperor near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a>. His reign lasted barely a year, a sign of how weak the Western Empire had become.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Yorkers topple George III's statue after the Declaration is read</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington had the Declaration read to his troops in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. That evening a crowd pulled down the gilded lead statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> on Bowling Green; much of the lead was later cast into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musket</a> balls.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1810">1810 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">216 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon annexes the Kingdom of Holland to France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after his brother Louis abdicated rather than enforce the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> of British trade, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> decreed Holland's annexation to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> independence was restored only in 1813.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1868">1868 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The 14th Amendment wins enough states for ratification</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>'s and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>'s approval gave the 14th Amendment the three-quarters of states it needed. It guaranteed citizenship to all born in the US and equal protection of the laws.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1877">1877 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first Wimbledon Championships begin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The All <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> Croquet and Lawn Tennis Club opened its first lawn tennis championship, with 22 men competing. Spencer Gore won the title ten days later, launching the world's oldest tennis tournament.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2011">2011 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">15 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">South Sudan becomes independent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-sudan">South Sudan</a> declared independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> after a referendum, becoming the world's newest internationally recognised state. Independence followed decades of civil war, but a new conflict erupted in 2013.</p></div></li></ol>
